How to install the /prototype command in Claude Code

This file teaches Claude Code a custom command called /prototype. Once installed, you can type /prototype in any Claude Code session and it will automatically load all the Page Builder guidelines, Figma links, and editorial rules — no copy-pasting required.

Step 1 — Find your home folder
On a Mac, open Finder. In the menu bar click Go → Home. This is your home folder (e.g. /Users/yourname).

Step 2 — Show hidden folders
Press Cmd+Shift+. (period) in Finder. This reveals hidden folders, including one called .claude.

Step 3 — Navigate to the commands folder
Open the .claude folder. Inside it, look for a folder called commands. If it doesn't exist, create it: File → New Folder, name it commands.

Step 4 — Add the file
Download or copy the prototype.md file from this repo and drag it into the commands folder.

Step 5 — Verify it works
Open Claude Code, type /prototype, and you should see it appear as an autocomplete option.
